meta {
  name: CreateResource — a git integration
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.ResourceService/CreateResource
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "kind": "KIND_INTEGRATION",
      "name": "org-github",
      "config": {
        "category": "git",
        "provider": "github",
        "base_url": "https://api.github.com"
      },
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0013, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  The category is a lowercase string — `git`, `task_manager` or `agent` — and not
  an enum: the one who rules the provider vocabulary is the provider (ADR-0009).

  It creates the integration WITHOUT a credential. The secret comes in through
  `SetCredential`, which writes it into the `SecretStore` and returns only the
  REFERENCE — the value never comes back in a read (ADR-0001).
}
